Status: NOT_STARTED - deferred backlog; do not begin without a new request.
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoyAdvance/issues/78
Milestone: Playable Nintendo DS beside the existing GBA on the desk.
Dependencies: None; retain the existing static-site and GBA behavior.

Purpose:
Add Nintendo DS emulation and a Nintendo DS console placed on the desk next
to the GBA. This is a future feature, not currently supported functionality.

Tasks:
- [ ] Evaluate a static-hostable DS core and document compatibility,
      licensing, browser requirements and any BIOS/firmware requirements.
- [ ] Add the Nintendo DS desk model next to the retained GBA.
- [ ] Define console selection and integrate DS loading, both screens,
      touchscreen input and the appropriate physical/keyboard/touch controls.
- [ ] Keep GBA/DS saves, active-game identity, cached ROMs and runtime
      lifecycle isolated; do not assume simultaneous emulation is required.
- [ ] Verify desktop and phone interaction using authorized fixtures, then
      update supported-system documentation and affected visual references.

Acceptance criteria:
Both consoles are present on the desk. Selecting the DS can load an
authorized NDS ROM into the matching dual-screen presentation, with working
touchscreen and button input. GBA loading, play and saves still work without
cross-system contamination. Hosting remains static; missing or unsupported
ROM/BIOS/firmware requirements produce explicit guidance rather than a false
success. Any required distributed assets have appropriate permission.

Completion evidence:
None. No DS core selection, asset research, model, runtime integration,
dependency change or compatibility testing has been started.

Completion log:
2026-11-06: Owner requests DS support and a second console beside the GBA,
but explicitly defers implementation. Record the workstream only.
